		},
		{
			"id": "0jsxlhNp",
			"type": "text",
			"x": -532.0478603430552,
			"y": 10294.267270358789,
			"width": 1645.438720703125,
			"height": 160,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "hachure",
			"strokeWidth": 1,
			"strokeStyle": "dashed",
			"roughness": 1,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "bCE",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 144954282,
			"version": 413,
			"versionNonce": 1621398838,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1775169942920,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "The real power comes from ZooKeeper's ability to notify all interested services when configuration changes. Imagine you want to enable a new feature across your entire chat platform. With ZooKeeper, you can:\n    - 1. Update a single ZNode: set /chat-app/config/enable_reactions \"true\"\n    - 2. All chat servers watching this node receive a notification\n    - 3. Servers update their behavior without restarting\n\nThis creates a powerful centralized configuration management because it enables real-time propagation, versioning, and atomic updates.\n\nHere's how an e-commerce platform might use ZooKeeper for configuration:",
			"rawText": "The real power comes from ZooKeeper's ability to notify all interested services when configuration changes. Imagine you want to enable a new feature across your entire chat platform. With ZooKeeper, you can:\n    - 1. Update a single ZNode: set /chat-app/config/enable_reactions \"true\"\n    - 2. All chat servers watching this node receive a notification\n    - 3. Servers update their behavior without restarting\n\nThis creates a powerful centralized configuration management because it enables real-time propagation, versioning, and atomic updates.\n\nHere's how an e-commerce platform might use ZooKeeper for configuration:",
			"fontSize": 16,
			"fontFamily": 5,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "The real power comes from ZooKeeper's ability to notify all interested services when configuration changes. Imagine you want to enable a new feature across your entire chat platform. With ZooKeeper, you can:\n    - 1. Update a single ZNode: set /chat-app/config/enable_reactions \"true\"\n    - 2. All chat servers watching this node receive a notification\n    - 3. Servers update their behavior without restarting\n\nThis creates a powerful centralized configuration management because it enables real-time propagation, versioning, and atomic updates.\n\nHere's how an e-commerce platform might use ZooKeeper for configuration:",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"link": null
		},
