			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1775169942920,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "ZooKeeper for Leader Election",
			"rawText": "ZooKeeper for Leader Election",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 5,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "ZooKeeper for Leader Election",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"link": null
		},
		{
			"id": "GDz7cksj",
			"type": "text",
			"x": -520.3370673378513,
			"y": 11836.439924351223,
			"width": 1979.638777019351,
			"height": 200,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "hachure",
			"strokeWidth": 1,
			"strokeStyle": "dashed",
			"roughness": 1,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "bCT",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 1427860714,
			"version": 740,
			"versionNonce": 1160435702,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1775169942920,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "In distributed systems, it's often necessary to designate one node as a \"leader\" responsible for certain operations. For example, you might want only one server to process payment transactions or schedule jobs. Having a leader allows you to coordinate\nthese operations and ensure only one server is doing them at a time.\n\nZooKeeper's sequential ZNodes make leader election straightforward:\n    1. Each server creates a sequential ephemeral node under a designated path\n    2. The server with the lowest sequence number becomes the leader\n    3. All other servers watch the node with the next lowest sequence number\n    4. If a leader fails, its node disappears, and the next server in sequence steps up\n\nHere's how it might look in our chat application if we wanted to elect a server to handle global announcements:",
			"rawText": "In distributed systems, it's often necessary to designate one node as a \"leader\" responsible for certain operations. For example, you might want only one server to process payment transactions or schedule jobs. Having a leader allows you to coordinate these operations and ensure only one server is doing them at a time.\n\nZooKeeper's sequential ZNodes make leader election straightforward:\n    1. Each server creates a sequential ephemeral node under a designated path\n    2. The server with the lowest sequence number becomes the leader\n    3. All other servers watch the node with the next lowest sequence number\n    4. If a leader fails, its node disappears, and the next server in sequence steps up\n\nHere's how it might look in our chat application if we wanted to elect a server to handle global announcements:",
			"fontSize": 16,
			"fontFamily": 5,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "In distributed systems, it's often necessary to designate one node as a \"leader\" responsible for certain operations. For example, you might want only one server to process payment transactions or schedule jobs. Having a leader allows you to coordinate these operations and ensure only one server is doing them at a time.\n\nZooKeeper's sequential ZNodes make leader election straightforward:\n    1. Each server creates a sequential ephemeral node under a designated path\n    2. The server with the lowest sequence number becomes the leader\n    3. All other servers watch the node with the next lowest sequence number\n    4. If a leader fails, its node disappears, and the next server in sequence steps up\n\nHere's how it might look in our chat application if we wanted to elect a server to handle global announcements:",
			"autoResize": false,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"link": null
		},
		{
			"id": "xBBwB1s0",
			"type": "text",
			"x": -503.8362163359361,
			"y": 12064.375442134287,
			"width": 648.203125,
			"height": 147.2,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "hachure",
			"strokeWidth": 1,
			"strokeStyle": "dashed",
			"roughness": 1,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "bCU",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 1773289386,
			"version": 438,
			"versionNonce": 490236214,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1775169942920,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "# Server 1 creates:\ncreate -s -e /chat-app/leader/node- \"server1\"  # Creates /chat-app/leader/node-0000000001\n\n# Server 2 creates:\ncreate -s -e /chat-app/leader/node- \"server2\"  # Creates /chat-app/leader/node-0000000002\n\n# Server 3 creates:\ncreate -s -e /chat-app/leader/node- \"server3\"  # Creates /chat-app/leader/node-0000000003",
			"rawText": "# Server 1 creates:\ncreate -s -e /chat-app/leader/node- \"server1\"  # Creates /chat-app/leader/node-0000000001\n\n# Server 2 creates:\ncreate -s -e /chat-app/leader/node- \"server2\"  # Creates /chat-app/leader/node-0000000002\n\n# Server 3 creates:\ncreate -s -e /chat-app/leader/node- \"server3\"  # Creates /chat-app/leader/node-0000000003",
			"fontSize": 16,
			"fontFamily": 2,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "# Server 1 creates:\ncreate -s -e /chat-app/leader/node- \"server1\"  # Creates /chat-app/leader/node-0000000001\n\n# Server 2 creates:\ncreate -s -e /chat-app/leader/node- \"server2\"  # Creates /chat-app/leader/node-0000000002\n\n# Server 3 creates:\ncreate -s -e /chat-app/leader/node- \"server3\"  # Creates /chat-app/leader/node-0000000003",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.15,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"link": null
		},
		{
			"id": "oi-ydjzQIKzqzdK-Rp8Fv",
			"type": "rectangle",
			"x": -520.0938635102034,
			"y": 12047.303590841373,
			"width": 686.5168220915359,
			"height": 187.46785479843123,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "hachure",
			"strokeWidth": 1,
			"strokeStyle": "dashed",
			"roughness": 1,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "bCV",
			"roundness": {
				"type": 3
			},
			"seed": 1365293674,
			"version": 550,
			"versionNonce": 1476514422,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1775169942920,
			"link": null,
			"locked": false,
			"hasTextLink": false
		},
		{
			"id": "jZpjYKAR",
			"type": "text",
			"x": -511.29094235730736,
			"y": 12276.863221141948,
			"width": 1850.3255260465749,
			"height": 140,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "hachure",
			"strokeWidth": 1,
			"strokeStyle": "dashed",
			"roughness": 1,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "bCW",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 452058410,
			"version": 503,
			"versionNonce": 1615598518,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1775169942920,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "Server 1 is now the leader since it has the lowest sequence number. Server 2 watches node-0000000001, and Server 3 watches node-0000000002. If Server 1 fails, its node disappears, Server 2 is notified and becomes the new leader,\nand Server 3 now watches Server 2.\n\nThis pattern allows for automatic failover and ensures only one server is performing the critical operation at any time.\n\nThe same approach is used in systems like HBase, where one server must coordinate schema changes, and in Kafka's earlier versions, where a controller broker manages partition leadership.\n",
			"rawText": "Server 1 is now the leader since it has the lowest sequence number. Server 2 watches node-0000000001, and Server 3 watches node-0000000002. If Server 1 fails, its node disappears, Server 2 is notified and becomes the new leader, and Server 3 now watches Server 2.\n\nThis pattern allows for automatic failover and ensures only one server is performing the critical operation at any time.\n\nThe same approach is used in systems like HBase, where one server must coordinate schema changes, and in Kafka's earlier versions, where a controller broker manages partition leadership.\n",
			"fontSize": 16,
			"fontFamily": 5,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "Server 1 is now the leader since it has the lowest sequence number. Server 2 watches node-0000000001, and Server 3 watches node-0000000002. If Server 1 fails, its node disappears, Server 2 is notified and becomes the new leader, and Server 3 now watches Server 2.\n\nThis pattern allows for automatic failover and ensures only one server is performing the critical operation at any time.\n\nThe same approach is used in systems like HBase, where one server must coordinate schema changes, and in Kafka's earlier versions, where a controller broker manages partition leadership.\n",
			"autoResize": false,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"link": null
		},
		{
			"id": "0UerkeLf",
			"type": "text",
			"x": -511.91481304562103,
			"y": 12567.804500317947,
			"width": 323.81976318359375,
			"height": 25,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "hachure",
			"strokeWidth": 1,
			"strokeStyle": "dashed",
			"roughness": 1,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "bCX",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 1137747946,
			"version": 377,
			"versionNonce": 3943670,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1775169942920,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "ZooKeeper for Distributed Locks",
			"rawText": "ZooKeeper for Distributed Locks",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 5,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "ZooKeeper for Distributed Locks",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"link": null
		},
		{
			"id": "GooF4wez",
			"type": "text",
			"x": -515.0447405666505,
			"y": 12640.638598139602,
			"width": 1438.447021484375,
			"height": 200,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "hachure",
			"strokeWidth": 1,
			"strokeStyle": "dashed",
			"roughness": 1,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "bCY",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 1678252714,
			"version": 362,
			"versionNonce": 1968643638,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1775169942920,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "Distributed locks allow multiple processes across different machines to coordinate access to shared resources. They're important for preventing race conditions in distributed systems.\n\nZooKeeper implements distributed locks using sequential ephemeral ZNodes:\n    1. Each client trying to acquire the lock creates a sequential ephemeral node under a lock path\n    2. All clients sort the nodes by sequence number\n    3. The client with the lowest sequence number holds the lock\n    4. Each client watches the node with the next lower sequence number\n    5. When a client releases the lock (or crashes), its ZNode is removed, and the next client is notified\n\nFor our chat application, imagine implementing rate limiting on message sending:",
			"rawText": "Distributed locks allow multiple processes across different machines to coordinate access to shared resources. They're important for preventing race conditions in distributed systems.\n\nZooKeeper implements distributed locks using sequential ephemeral ZNodes:\n    1. Each client trying to acquire the lock creates a sequential ephemeral node under a lock path\n    2. All clients sort the nodes by sequence number\n    3. The client with the lowest sequence number holds the lock\n    4. Each client watches the node with the next lower sequence number\n    5. When a client releases the lock (or crashes), its ZNode is removed, and the next client is notified\n\nFor our chat application, imagine implementing rate limiting on message sending:",
			"fontSize": 16,
			"fontFamily": 5,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "Distributed locks allow multiple processes across different machines to coordinate access to shared resources. They're important for preventing race conditions in distributed systems.\n\nZooKeeper implements distributed locks using sequential ephemeral ZNodes:\n    1. Each client trying to acquire the lock creates a sequential ephemeral node under a lock path\n    2. All clients sort the nodes by sequence number\n    3. The client with the lowest sequence number holds the lock\n    4. Each client watches the node with the next lower sequence number\n    5. When a client releases the lock (or crashes), its ZNode is removed, and the next client is notified\n\nFor our chat application, imagine implementing rate limiting on message sending:",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"link": null
		},
		{
			"id": "fYlKGaFu",
			"type": "text",
			"x": -509.1972746236456,
			"y": 12871.757792547018,
			"width": 770.8984375,
			"height": 184,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "hachure",
			"strokeWidth": 1,
			"strokeStyle": "dashed",
			"roughness": 1,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "bCZ",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 1514354026,
			"version": 329,
			"versionNonce": 75622262,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1775169942920,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "# Client 1 wants to send a message:\ncreate -s -e /chat-app/locks/send_message- \"client1\"  # Creates /chat-app/locks/send_message-0000000001\n\n# Client 2 also wants to send:\ncreate -s -e /chat-app/locks/send_message- \"client2\"  # Creates /chat-app/locks/send_message-0000000002\n\n# Client 1 sends its message, then deletes its node\ndelete /chat-app/locks/send_message-0000000001\n\n# Client 2 is notified and now holds the lock",
			"rawText": "# Client 1 wants to send a message:\ncreate -s -e /chat-app/locks/send_message- \"client1\"  # Creates /chat-app/locks/send_message-0000000001\n\n# Client 2 also wants to send:\ncreate -s -e /chat-app/locks/send_message- \"client2\"  # Creates /chat-app/locks/send_message-0000000002\n\n# Client 1 sends its message, then deletes its node\ndelete /chat-app/locks/send_message-0000000001\n\n# Client 2 is notified and now holds the lock",
			"fontSize": 16,
			"fontFamily": 2,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "# Client 1 wants to send a message:\ncreate -s -e /chat-app/locks/send_message- \"client1\"  # Creates /chat-app/locks/send_message-0000000001\n\n# Client 2 also wants to send:\ncreate -s -e /chat-app/locks/send_message- \"client2\"  # Creates /chat-app/locks/send_message-0000000002\n\n# Client 1 sends its message, then deletes its node\ndelete /chat-app/locks/send_message-0000000001\n\n# Client 2 is notified and now holds the lock",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.15,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"link": null
		},
		{
